 "summary": "Logs the resolved canonical path alongside the configured data directory path during startup logging if the paths differ. If the data directory or any parent path contains a symlink, the target location is appended to the log output.",
 "problem": "When the data directory involves symlinks, startup logs only print the configured path, obscuring the physical storage location (such as an SSD versus HDD) used during a run.",
 "evidence": [
  "Author description: 'This patch would mostly help developers. I've been testing a potential performance PR across different data directories (for example, SSD versus HDD)... changing the startup command arguments may be inconvenient or not even possible. But it's easy to change the default directory to be a symlink.'"
